  "625:0 metadata-line Valid HTML entity references and numeric character reference",
  "626:0 metadata-line can be used in place of the corresponding Unicode character,",
  "627:0 metadata-line with the following exceptions:",
  "629:0 metadata-line - Entity and character references are not recognized in code",
  "630:0 metadata-line   blocks and code spans.",
  "632:0 metadata-line - Entity and character references cannot stand in place of",
  "633:0 metadata-line   special characters that define structural elements in",
  "634:0 metadata-line   CommonMark.  For example, although \`&#42;\` can be used",
  "635:0 metadata-line   in place of a literal \`*\` character, \`&#42;\` cannot replac",
  "636:0 metadata-line   \`*\` in emphasis delimiters, bullet list markers, or themat",
  "637:0 metadata-line   breaks.",
  "639:0 metadata-line Conforming CommonMark parsers need not store information abo",
  "640:0 metadata-line whether a particular character was represented in the source",
  "641:0 metadata-line using a Unicode character or an entity reference.",
  "643:0 metadata-line [Entity references](@) consist of \`&\` + any of the valid",
  "644:0 metadata-line HTML5 entity names + \`;\`. The",
  "645:0 metadata-line document <https://html.spec.whatwg.org/entities.json>",
  "646:0 metadata-line is used as an authoritative source for the valid entity",
  "647:0 metadata-line references and their corresponding code points.",
